// Key Vault key inventory by algorithm family - Azure Resource Graph.
//
// Run against Azure Resource Graph (portal, az graph query, Resource Graph
// Explorer), not Sentinel. ARG speaks a KQL subset over the `resources` table.
// Schema status: [inference] property paths verified against documentation and
// the ARM representation of Microsoft.KeyVault/vaults/keys; confirm on one
// subscription before running tenant-wide.
//
// Why include a control-plane query in a detection folder: HNDL exposure lives
// in stored key material as much as in traffic. Key Vault is one of the few
// places where an organisation's asymmetric keys are enumerable at all,
// programmatically, with no agent. It is also the estate that a passive
// certificate assessment provably cannot see - see the README section on what
// this assessment will not tell you.
//
// Note that key listing requires the key metadata to be exposed to ARG; keys
// in vaults with restricted RBAC will silently not appear. Absence here is not
// evidence of absence in the vault.

resources
| where type =~ "microsoft.keyvault/vaults/keys"
| extend kty = tostring(properties.kty)
| extend keySize = toint(properties.keySize)
| extend curve = tostring(properties.curveName)
| extend enabled = tobool(properties.attributes.enabled)
| extend expires = todatetime(properties.attributes.exp)
| extend QuantumVulnerable = kty in~ ("RSA", "RSA-HSM", "EC", "EC-HSM")
| extend OutlivesMilestone = isnull(expires) or expires > datetime(2030-12-31)
| summarize
    Keys = count(),
    Vaults = dcount(split(id, "/")[8]),
    NoExpirySet = countif(isnull(expires))
  by kty, keySize, curve, QuantumVulnerable, OutlivesMilestone, subscriptionId
| order by Keys desc
// NoExpirySet is the crypto-agility tell worth reading first: a key with no
// expiry is a key nobody has planned to rotate, which makes it a key nobody has
// planned to migrate.
